# UI System Architecture

Before planning or changing shared primitives, forms, dialogs, sheets,
drawers, navigation, accessibility behavior, responsive layout, or page-level
information architecture, read:

- `docs/architecture/ui-system-and-responsive-layout.md`

Treat that document as binding repository guidance. In particular:

- Use shadcn/Radix for generic accessible behavior, but preserve documented
  Upwards-specific extensions and product components.
- Do not overwrite customized primitives with registry source without reviewing
  and preserving their behavior.
- Do not add raw generic controls when a shared primitive fits.
- Every touch or pointer interaction needs a keyboard-accessible equivalent.
- The app is phone-only. A wide window shows a notice and a 430px frame with
  the same layout. Do not add a sidebar, a two-column page, or a `md:`/`lg:`
  layout variant.
- Preserve the mobile PWA experience. It is the product.

Any intentional departure must update the architecture document and explain
the changed product tradeoff before implementation.
